<title>CANADA: Air Canada pockets US$154 mln from shr sale.</title>
<headline>Air Canada pockets US$154 mln from shr sale.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air Canada said on Thursday it sold its remaining 5.6 million class B shares in Continental Airlines for proceeds of US$154 million.</p>
<p>Air Canada said the sale represented a before-tax income of over C$170 million for the airline -- a 550 percent gain on the original investment made in 1993 -- which would be used to pay down debt.</p>
<p>The carrier, Canada's largest, said the sale of its Continental equity stake would not affect the two airlines' commercial alliance.</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
